// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: the adopted literal's boxed field where THREE sources disagree about
// the payload's atom. Three lines. It is its predecessor's program with ONE token changed —
// `i32` became `i64` — and that one token is the whole row.
//
// `vl check` exits 0 with NO DIAGNOSTICS AT ALL and is the ONLY command that misses it;
// `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl check --codegen --no-validate` exits 0, `vl build`
// writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected i32, found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed.)
//
// THE MECHANISM, AND WHY IT IS NOT ITS PREDECESSOR'S. `structIndexOfObjCtx` adopts `Circle`'s
// row for the un-annotated `{ r: 7 }` — that much is shared, and closing it at the read is
// what D209's three-rung channel does. Here the adoption ALSO WIDENS: the field's declared
// member is `i64`, so the store boxes the payload as tag 3 / `struct.new $vbI64`, while the
// CHECKER types the read `i32`. Three sources — declared member, stored payload, checker type
// — and no two of them agree. Unbox to i32 and the `ref.cast $vbI32` faces an `$vbI64`
// payload; unbox to i64 and `print`, typed `i32` by the checker, receives an i64.
//
// WHY THIS ONE — AND THE PROPERTY IS A CENSUS, NOT AN ARGUMENT. The slot turned over twice in
// one day (D282 → D209 → D224, and D224 closed before it could be taken), so this successor
// was chosen by RUNNING every row of `silent-class-inventory.md` against this tree rather than
// by reasoning about which family a program belongs to. All 136 rows' own filed programs were
// graded; exactly ONE is `check-clean invalid wasm`, and it is the row this commit closes.
// **This is the only live member of the class that remains.** It is not chosen over
// alternatives — it is what is left, which is the one selection rule that cannot be wrong
// about the population.
//
// IT ALSO INHERITS THE PROPERTY ITS PREDECESSOR WAS CHOSEN FOR: it DECLARES NO UNION, so
// `uVariants` is empty, `armLayoutContested` is false, `variantStructHeapTwinAt` and
// `uVarSTwin` are never called, and `emitUnionCoerce` is unreachable. Every mechanism of the
// variant⇄struct family (D33 / D139 / D156 / D158 / D171 / D224 / D280 / D282) is structurally
// inapplicable.
//
// AND THE CAVEAT IS STATED RATHER THAN GLOSSED, because the last two selection rules each
// failed within a day of being written. This program is NOT out of reach of the mechanism that
// just closed its sibling. D209's channel predicate SEES it and declines — counted at the site
// as `reach=1 ans=0` — on its third condition, "the box can actually HOLD the checker's atom".
// Drop that condition and this row closes, and 36 cells of the `d272` grid redden with it
// (that is exactly the `R alone` column of D209's ablation table). It survives on a MEASURED
// refusal, which is the same class of evidence D224 had when its 199-cell price turned out to
// be a bundle of 134 + 65. Read the price, not the silence.
//
// THERE IS NO NAMED SUCCESSOR, and that is the honest state rather than an omission: after this
// file, `silent-class-inventory.md` has no other row whose filed repro is check-clean invalid
// wasm and the corpus carries no other `@no-instantiate` directive. WHEN THIS CLOSES, re-run
// the census (`vl check` + `vl run` over every row's own repro) before assuming the class
// refilled — and if it has not, set `INVALID_MODULE_SRC = null` and let the announced-inactive
// path in `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` do its job rather than reaching for a program that
// is not really in the class.
//
// PRE-EXISTING, MEASURED RATHER THAN INHERITED: graded `check-clean invalid wasm` on this
// change's merge base (seed 1,463,129) and on its shipped seed (1,463,730), the same sentence
// both times, and its module is BYTE-IDENTICAL across the change (274 bytes, `cmp`-equal).
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty.
type Circle = { r: i64 | null }
const lv1 = [{ r: 7 }]
print((lv1[0]).r)
